  "_comment": "icraft override of betterdeserttemples:main processor_list (jar default: YungsBetterDesertTemples-1.20-Forge-3.0.3.jar -> data/betterdeserttemples/worldgen/processor_list/main.json). EVERY YUNG temple template-pool element references this single list via \"processors\": \"betterdeserttemples:main\", so it is the one place to inject a structure-wide block swap. WHAT CHANGED: prepended a single minecraft:rule processor that rewrites minecraft:trapped_chest -> minecraft:chest (operator request: temple chests should be NORMAL, not trapped). The 25 original YUNG processors are preserved verbatim and unchanged after it. WHY THIS PRESERVES LOOT: vanilla 1.20.1 RuleProcessor.processBlock (verified against client-1.20.1 RuleProcessor bytecode) constructs the output StructureBlockInfo with ProcessorRule.applyRule(random, blockInfo.nbt()); when a rule has no output_nbt it returns the SOURCE block-entity nbt unchanged -> the chest's LootTable tag (betterdeserttemples:chests/*) survives the swap, so the swapped normal chest still rolls loot. STATE COVERAGE: across all 197 temple .nbt templates, trapped_chest only ever appears as [facing=east,type=single,waterlogged=false]; the 4 facing rules below are exhaustive + future-proof and each maps to the identical normal-chest state so orientation/double-chest pairing is preserved. RELOAD-SAFE: pure datapack JSON, applied on world (re)generation; existing already-generated chests are unaffected (they were placed before this processor existed).",
